pe/checkbox] [:db/add "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c" :answer-field/choices "290959aa-c9e0-552a-b454-bf5b41e57491"] [:db/add "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c" :answer-field/choices "6d0b566c-e3b7-52ff-95cf-90860925fada"] [:db/add "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c" :answer-field/correct "6d0b566c-e3b7-52ff-95cf-90860925fada"] [:db/ensure "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/id #uuid "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3"] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\mid {x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + {x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ is true. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A\\text{ is not invertible}$ only."] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/answer-fields "62ecaf89-7f8c-5743-8190-377e5b4987a1"] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/answer-fields "460aa660-c8cb-5c14-a7a7-344c954cf7ea"] [:db/add "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/answer-fields "1e751ad0-31b9-5191-b323-5b7b0e2bc46c"] [:db/ensure "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/questions "c254c2c5-fa4e-5e1f-9d05-d1929805dcd3"] [:db/add "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794" :answer/id #uuid "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794"] [:db/add "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794" :answer/value "I and II only"] [:db/ensure "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794" :answer/validate] [:db/add "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da" :answer/id #uuid "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da"] [:db/add "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da" :answer/value "II only"] [:db/ensure "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da" :answer/validate] [:db/add "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8" :answer/id #uuid "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8"] [:db/add "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8" :answer/value "I only"] [:db/ensure "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8" :answer/validate] [:db/add "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024" :answer/id #uuid "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024"] [:db/add "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024" :answer/value "III only"] [:db/ensure "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024" :answer/validate] [:db/add "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77" :answer/id #uuid "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77"] [:db/add "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77" :answer/value "II and III only"] [:db/ensure "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/choices "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/choices "11d72e44-a033-5788-b049-8a451dbad1da"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/choices "1522bd23-2fc5-5e8e-81c9-c3ca0adfaab8"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/choices "7226ecd6-8273-51ac-aea6-43a3c8e77024"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/choices "2bbf6eaf-1e5c-54f5-b3b7-442da6545e77"] [:db/add "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/correct "37ae6200-8724-50c0-b709-2ecc0e3f8794"] [:db/ensure "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/id #uuid "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc"] [:db/add "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\mid {x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$\n\nII. $A\\text{ is not invertible}$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$"] [:db/add "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + {x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2$. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\n- Statement II is true: $A\\text{ is not invertible}$. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false: $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne \\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only."] [:db/add "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/answer-fields "a8de8536-0c81-5998-87eb-81d60e006561"] [:db/ensure "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/questions "4d55ab29-1e9c-54fa-b4c5-045bb2cab9cc"] [:db/add "7b672e0b-ae46-5880-be16-e1113fcc04e4" :answer/id #uuid "7b672e0b-ae46-5880-be16-e1113fcc04e4"] [:db/add "7b672e0b-ae46-5880-be16-e1113fcc04e4" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "7b672e0b-ae46-5880-be16-e1113fcc04e4" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "7b672e0b-ae46-5880-be16-e1113fcc04e4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "c085a98d-898b-5d44-94d1-63ede2e82e2d" :answer/id #uuid "c085a98d-898b-5d44-94d1-63ede2e82e2d"] [:db/add "c085a98d-898b-5d44-94d1-63ede2e82e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "c085a98d-898b-5d44-94d1-63ede2