ution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe supplied nullspace can be written as the span of the independent vectors in\n\n$${x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$$\n\nHence $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$. In particular, $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is false. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4$ is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$; $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4$ only."] [:db/add "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b" :question/answer-fields "35642cd1-9c6c-5719-b955-e0c0c6035e72"] [:db/add "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b" :question/answer-fields "1ae79cff-5786-59fd-8689-3572a75aa7ee"] [:db/add "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b" :question/answer-fields "79426dc1-d4e1-5869-bb3a-e61c0a7fc4d6"] [:db/ensure "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/questions "11e6dd5d-7bfa-519f-8ed0-b83419e1cc9b"] [:db/add "1def3aa4-ca90-5a60-ae81-18f879b8fddb" :answer/id #uuid "1def3aa4-ca90-5a60-ae81-18f879b8fddb"] [:db/add "1def3aa4-ca90-5a60-ae81-18f879b8fddb" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "1def3aa4-ca90-5a60-ae81-18f879b8fddb" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "1def3aa4-ca